  "term": "mortality effect",
  "definition": "Mortality effect is the death-producing impact of an exposure or agent, measured by how much mortality it causes and when that mortality occurs. In this source, it refers to broflanilide causing a dose-dependent and delayed increase in mosquito deaths after exposure.",
